{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "1CH",
 "chapter": 2,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.3",
   "range": "1CH.2.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "01ddfce6",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.3#p1-01ddfce6",
     "text": "Though Judah was not Jacob's eldest son, yet he first begins with him, because he would come to the genealogy of David, of whom came Christ.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "Judah"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.6",
   "range": "1CH.2.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "d0bcaefb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.6#p1-d0bcaefb",
     "text": "Of these read 1Ki 4:31.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "Ethan",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ki 4:31",
       "ref": "1KI.4.31"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.9",
   "range": "1CH.2.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fddad57a",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.9#p1-fddad57a",
     "text": "Whom Matthew calls Aram, Mt 1:3.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "Ram",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mt 1:3",
       "ref": "MAT.1.3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.10",
   "range": "1CH.2.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "43533286",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.10#p1-43533286",
     "text": "That is, chief of the family.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "prince of the children of Judah"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.18",
   "range": "1CH.2.18",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "874cb019",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.18#p1-874cb019",
     "text": "Who was called Chelubai the son of Hezron, 1Ch 2:9.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "Caleb the son of Hezron begat",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 2:9",
       "ref": "1CH.2.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.21",
   "range": "1CH.2.21",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8de4449d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.21#p1-8de4449d",
     "text": "Who was prince of mount Gilead, Nu 32:40.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "Gilead",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Nu 32:40",
       "ref": "NUM.32.40"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.23",
   "range": "1CH.2.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "9687a0a4",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.23#p1-9687a0a4",
     "text": "That is, the Geshurites and Syrians took the towns from Jair's children.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "from them"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.24",
   "range": "1CH.2.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "5d8b6f4a",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.24#p1-5ce0eae3",
     "text": "Which was a town named for the husband and wife, also called Bethlehem Ephratah.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "Calebephratah"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.24#p2-063ba3f9",
     "text": "Meaning, the chief and prince.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "father of Tekoa"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.31",
   "range": "1CH.2.31",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b2739cc4",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.31#p1-b2739cc4",
     "text": "Who died while his father was alive, and therefore it is said in 1Ch 2:34 that Sheshan had no sons.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "Ahlai",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ch 2:34",
       "ref": "1CH.2.34"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.42",
   "range": "1CH.2.42",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6964265f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.42#p1-6964265f",
     "text": "That is, the chief governor or prince of the Ziphims, because the prince should have a fatherly care and affection for his people.",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "father of Ziph"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.46",
   "range": "1CH.2.46",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fcea0cf3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.46#p1-fcea0cf3",
     "text": "The difference between the wife and the concubine was that the wife was taken with a ceremony of marriage and her children inherited, while the concubine had no marriage ceremony, neither did her children inherit, but had a portion of goods or money given to them.",
     "label": "m",
     "anchor": "concubine"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.54",
   "range": "1CH.2.54",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "47500efc",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.54#p1-47500efc",
     "text": "The chief and principle of the house of Joab.",
     "label": "n",
     "anchor": "house of Joab"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/1CH.2.55",
   "range": "1CH.2.55",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "3a90255a",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.55#p1-f28c1582",
     "text": "Who were men learned and expert in the law.",
     "label": "o",
     "anchor": "scribes which dwelt at Jabez"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/1CH.2.55#p2-e4eae4bb",
     "text": "Read Nu 10:29, Jud 1:16.",
     "label": "p",
     "anchor": "Kenites that came of Hemath",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Nu 10:29, Jud 1:16",
       "ref": "NUM.10.29"
      },
      {
       "text": "Nu 10:29, Jud 1:16",
       "ref": "JDG.1.16"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
